{"id":"52227c89f495304654c16aec609c911f59a9297256307f702657237a601ffa7f","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-11-08T20:21:42.799023963Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## Parent\n\nSub-issue of 215ee3.\n\n## What to build\n\nDeleting a ticket writes an explicit Operation instead of removing its keys, so a Deletion is never confused with a Stranded index and travels to every clone. Two op kinds, delete (optional reason) and undelete; a ticket is deleted iff the highest (lamport, id) op among those two is delete, so Deletion wins over concurrent edits. Keys stay (soft deletion), format-version stays 2. `ti delete` keeps its confirmation UX, writes the op, touches no parent or dependency sets. New `ti undelete <id>`. `ti list` hides deleted tickets; `ti list --deleted` shows only them. `ti show` on a deleted ticket exits 0 and renders a Deleted banner with when and by whom; `--json` carries `deleted: {at, by} | null` on every ticket. `ti checkout` refuses a deleted ticket, non-zero. JSON schema v1 extended additively. Agent docs and release notes state that older binaries show deleted tickets as alive and should be upgraded.\n\nOlder binaries: unknown op kinds are skipped on replay, so ti <= 0.4.2 sees the ticket alive. Accepted; bumping format-version would abort `ti list` on old clones.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Op-log unit tests: delete/undelete ordering by (lamport, id); replay with delete last yields deleted; unknown-kind skip test still passes\n- [ ] CLI: `ti delete` then `ti list` hides it; `ti list --deleted` shows only it; `ti show` prints Deleted banner, exit 0; `ti show --json` has `deleted.at`/`deleted.by`; `ti checkout` refused non-zero\n- [ ] CLI: `ti undelete` restores: visible in list, comments, tags, parent and dependencies intact without any relink\n- [ ] Two-clone CLI test: delete in A, sync both; B hides it; comment in B before B syncs lands on hidden ticket and is visible after undelete\n- [ ] `ti delete` writes no set changes on parent or dependency tickets\n- [ ] Schema `docs/schema/v1.json` extended; schema test green\n- [ ] Agent docs and release notes mention old-binary ghosts and upgrade"}}}